# Cloudflare Pages cache headers.
# 24/jul: fixes production bug where a stale cached index.html referenced
# JS chunk filenames deleted by a newer deploy ("Failed to fetch dynamically
# imported module" -> blank page). Hashed asset filenames change on every
# build, so they're safe to cache forever; index.html must always be
# revalidated so it never points at deleted chunks.
#
# 24/jul, round 2 (real root cause found in production, happened 2x): in the
# ~30-60s window right after a deploy while Cloudflare replicates new chunks
# to edge POPs, a request for /assets/*.js can get served the SPA-fallback
# HTML instead of the real JS file. Cache Level Standard then caches that
# WRONG response per-cookie (e.g. per GA cookie) -- so anyone who hits that
# race window during the replication gap gets stuck with a cached blank
# page until a manual Purge Everything. Two layers against it: _routes.json
# excludes /assets/* from Pages' SPA routing (so a miss 404s instead of
# silently falling back to index.html), and Vary: Accept-Encoding here
# (deliberately not Vary: Cookie) keeps the cache key off cookie identity.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Vary: Accept-Encoding
